1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:05,729
Hi everyone, welcome back to my channel. This week we are going to be talking about feeling like an outcast.
大家好，欢迎回来。这周聊聊觉得自己不合群的感受。

2
00:00:05,739 --> 00:00:10,839
Specifically for those who just constantly feel like they don't belong, almost like you're born an outcast.
尤其是那些经常觉得自己不属于哪里、仿佛天生就不合群的人。

3
00:00:10,839 --> 00:00:14,310
This is something that I want to talk about because I've dealt with it my whole life.
我想聊这件事，因为一直在经历它。

4
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:22,720
Being born Asian American, as a kid being shy, introverted, growing up ugly, um, I didn't have any friends and people wouldn't really approach me.
作为亚裔美国人，我小时候害羞、内向，也对外貌没自信，朋友不多，别人也不太主动找我。

5
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:27,160
And I remember just doing a lot of times in middle school, I would just sit alone at a lunch table.
我记得中学时，有很多次都是一个人坐在午餐桌旁。

6
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:33,390
I would bring a book and basically pretend that I'm reading to not look like, to not feel like a loser.
我会带本书，假装在读，好让自己看起来、感觉上没那么尴尬。

7
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:37,419
And I would have a few friends, but sometimes like if they're not there I would just read.
也有几个朋友，但如果他们不在，我就自己看书。

8
00:00:37,419 --> 00:00:45,160
I didn't have like the popular, you know, the popular girls clothes, Amber. Uggs were a huge thing. North Face jackets were a huge thing. I didn't have those.
我没有当时受欢迎的女孩们常穿的衣服，比如流行的靴子和外套。

9
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:52,420
So there was an appearance wise when I was younger, and then when I got older it was the anxiety aspect of it, like especially in social settings.
小时候更多是外表上的不安，长大后则更多是社交场合的紧张。

10
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:59,910
I don't know how people just go very smoothly. There's people who have a lot of connections at these social events, and they would just go up to people and just go, hey, what's up?
我不知道别人怎么能那么自如。有些人在活动中认识很多人，会自然走上前打招呼。

11
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:05,379
Remember there was this once back in like freshman year of college, they said this upperclassmen when I was walking back from class.
记得大一有一次，下课往回走时，有位高年级学生和我说话。

12
00:01:05,379 --> 00:01:09,040
And she was like, oh, you should come to this party. And I was like, I was a freshman, I was like, yeah, sure, why not?
她说，来这个聚会吧。我当时才大一，就想，好呀，试试看。

13
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:14,080
I went there. I literally stood there. Everyone's like taking shots and I was scared and want to take a shot.
去了之后，我只是站着。大家在喝酒，我有点害怕，不知道该怎么参与。

14
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:20,140
And I was there and I just felt so outcasted. Everyone was talking. I stood there, people looked at me and nobody wanted to approach me.
大家都在聊天，我站在那里，感觉自己被孤立了，也没人主动来找我说话。

15
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:28,890
It wasn't social. And also at that period of time I didn't really dress up and I didn't seem inviting, I guess. I was really stiff there.
那时我也不太会社交，不怎么打扮，可能看上去不好接近，整个人很拘谨。

16
00:01:31,619 --> 00:01:36,940
I have been in friend groups, but the thing was not they do get toxic towards the end, I would say.
我也有过朋友圈，但有些关系到后来会让我感觉不太健康。

17
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:42,940
I remember like when I was in frank groups, I felt really, really trapped. Like I feel like I can't go meet other people.
记得有时身处朋友圈反而很受束缚，好像不能再去认识别人。

18
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:48,390
I don't have a current friend group right now. Yeah, it feels lonely and it just feels like you don't belong. You don't belong anywhere.
现在我没有固定朋友圈，会感到孤独，好像哪里都不属于自己。

19
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:53,920
Like you know people that can just like text their friends and be, hey, can you, we like just hang out? I don't have that friend group anymore.
有些人能随时给朋友发消息约着见面，我现在没有那样的圈子了。

20
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:57,880
I'm like friends with individual people because for me I feel that that causes less drama.
我更多是分别和不同的人交朋友，感觉这样少一些关系里的纷争。

21
00:01:57,880 --> 00:02:04,179
When there's arguments within friend groups, it can end up really badly. And that's happened to me before and I don't want that to happen again.
朋友圈里起争执，有时会闹得很不好。我经历过，不想再发生。

22
00:02:04,179 --> 00:02:09,160
And I guess like this is why people are in relationships, because it makes them feel like they belong. They belong to another person.
我想，有些人进入亲密关系，也许是为了感到有归属、有连接。

23
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:14,140
Oh, maybe that's a bad way to, but you guys know what I mean. They have this connection with this other person. They're always going to be there for them, right?
也许这样说不太准确，但你明白我的意思，就是和某个人有连接，感觉对方会陪着自己。

24
00:02:14,140 --> 00:02:19,589
For me it's just, I, I don't have that. This has always been my entire life. I'm always on my own little island.
对我来说，我没有这样的感觉，好像一直都在自己的小岛上。

25
00:02:19,599 --> 00:02:25,360
Everyone is, you know, in groups and groups and groups and groups and groups and groups and groups, and I'm just in my own little island right here.
别人都在一个又一个群体里，而我还是在自己的小岛上。

26
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:29,200
And it gets lonely because I feel like as a human everyone craves connection.
会孤单，因为我觉得人都渴望与别人建立连接。

27
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:38,860
So then usually when you don't belong, you would try to fit in, and whether that's like changing your appearance or, you know, changing your personality or, you know, whatever it is.
感觉不合群时，人可能就会试着改变外表、改变表现，努力融入。

28
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:43,840
I've done that. I've changed my appearance. But also I will say that I changed my appearance due to myself, like self care.
我也做过这些，改变过外表。当然也有为了照顾自己、让自己舒服的部分。

29
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:48,220
But a part of it was also I want to fit in. I want people to like me. I want to make friends.
但也有一部分是想融入，希望别人喜欢我，想交朋友。

30
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:52,780
And then I also change my personality, which I would link the video right here where I talked about growing up ugly.
我也改变过性格表现，之前有支讲成长经历的视频谈到过。

31
00:02:52,780 --> 00:03:01,539
I was very introverted and I'm also extroverted in some aspects, but I, you know, amplified it. I tried to become more extrovert than I am and it was hard to keep up.
我本来比较内向，也有外向的一面，但把那一面放大后，很难一直维持。

32
00:03:01,539 --> 00:03:06,280
The needs of constantly wanting to fit in but at the same time you just don't fit in with exhausting.
一直想融入，却又觉得融不进去，真的很累。

33
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:08,379
Or maybe it could also just be I haven't found the right people.
也许只是我还没找到真正合得来的人。

34
00:03:08,379 --> 00:03:13,120
Which goes to my next poem, which is the fact that I just have to stop trying to fit in. I really stopped trying to fit in.
这就说到下一点：我想停止勉强自己融入，也真的开始这么做了。

35
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:16,720
And one of the prime examples of me not trying to fit in is posting on social media.
我不再强求融入的一个例子，就是开始在社交媒体发内容。

36
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:21,099
Back then when I was just so scared to post on social media because I thought of what people think of me.
以前我不敢发，总担心别人怎么看。

37
00:03:21,099 --> 00:03:26,319
What really got me through it was the fact that I didn't fit it in the first place, so who cares if I post on social media?
后来我想，本来也没融入，发点自己喜欢的又怎样呢？

38
00:03:26,319 --> 00:03:31,179
I'm not gonna like lose a bunch of friends because I did have a lot of friends to begin and with. True friends will stay by me.
我想不用因为发内容就担心失去朋友，真正的朋友会支持我。

39
00:03:31,179 --> 00:03:36,220
And so at the end just be unapologetically yourself. That's what I learned because fitting in is so exhausting.
所以，我学到的是自然做自己，不必总为自己是谁感到抱歉，因为硬要融入太累了。
